  "answer": "The figure comparing unemployment among women in Illinois and Michigan is now on screen in your browser tab. It's the \"Unemployment - Women Trends\" line chart on America's Health Rankings' State Comparison page, covering 2017–2024. It plots the percentage of the female civilian workforce that is unemployed, with Illinois as circles and Michigan as squares.\n\n- **Overall pattern:** The two states track each other closely, both peaking near 9.7% in 2020.\n- **Recent years:** They separate slightly after 2020, with Illinois ending a bit higher in 2024. Roughly 4.4% for Illinois and 3.7% for Michigan, read off the chart.\n- **Source:** The data comes from the Bureau of Labor Statistics' Local Area Unemployment Statistics program.\n\nI closed the survey pop-up and left the page as is, with the chart visible.",
